      "The Glossary terms opened counter on your account is now a way in: press it and you get the list of every term you have opened, newest first, with the date you met it and a box to filter them. Click any of them to read it again.",
      "For those with the editor: it opens on a new Dashboard of Folio in numbers — the cards, decks, glossary and citations counted out of the files themselves, and the accounts, shared decks and messages counted out of the database. And a card now belongs to one deck rather than to any number of them, so the deck picker chooses instead of ticking.",
      "A hundred and forty-four new glossary terms, and now every card has an entry for its own answer, so the word you are asked to remember can always be looked up. Sixty-eight are on the Old Stone Age — its divisions, the toolmaking traditions that fill it, the painted caves and dig sites that made it, the regions the story runs through and how any of it gets dated — and the rest on the early Holocene, the Aegean Bronze Age, the first humans out of Africa, the peopling of the Americas and the warm and cold ages that followed. Each lists the works behind it and points at them sentence by sentence. Many more spellings now open a popup when you meet them in a card; two terms reachable under a name belonging to something else no longer answer to it; and one left without a lifespan or a career, because the only works giving them were encyclopedias, now has both. And a card no longer offers a link to the very word it has just asked you to remember.",
